# Build
node_modules/
dist/
*.tsbuildinfo
.turbo/
coverage/

# Derived: `pnpm screenshots` writes here, and a PNG is not a diff anyone reads.
docs/screenshots/

# The `.vsix` and the tree it is packaged from (`pnpm package:vsix`). Both are
# build output; the script and the manifest are what get reviewed.
packages/vscode/.vsix/
*.vsix

# `pnpm test:host` — the editor it downloads, and the CommonJS build of the
# suite it runs inside it.
.vscode-test/
packages/vscode/dist-host/

# Axiomap's own output.
#
# Unanchored (`**/`) rather than §5's root-relative form, because Phase 6 gave
# this repo a working CLI and the first thing anyone does with it is point it at
# `fixtures/defi`. A pattern containing a slash is anchored to this file's
# directory, so `.axiomap/cache/` would have covered a `.axiomap/` at the root
# and nothing under `fixtures/` — where every `axiomap build` in this repo
# actually writes.
**/.axiomap/graph.json
**/.axiomap/cache/
**/.axiomap/findings.json
# NOT .axiomap/review.json — that is meant to be shared

# Compiler output in the fixtures, except the build-info that Phase 3's
# semantic tier reads. Per-contract artifacts are ~1 MB of bytecode this repo
# has no use for; `out/build-info/*.json` is the standard-JSON input+output pair
# and is committed on purpose, so the semantic tier has something to read in CI
# on a machine with no solc.
fixtures/*/out/*
!fixtures/*/out/build-info/
fixtures/*/cache/

# Generated perf fixture — `node fixtures/large/generate.mjs` reproduces it
# byte-identically from a fixed seed. ~8 MB of derived Solidity; the generator
# is the fixture, not its output.
fixtures/large/generated/

# Never
fixtures/client/
*.sol.private
.env*
